---
description: Draft, validate, and commit the end-of-phase session status
---

Produce the end-of-phase status for this repository.

## Step 1 - Friction summary (you, not the subagent)

From your own context in THIS session, write a short friction summary: denied
or reverted actions, retry loops, dependency problems, anything that cost time
or nearly went wrong. Be specific and honest; include things that reflect badly
on the session. If nothing notable happened, say so explicitly.

You are the only party with this information - the subagent cannot recover it.

## Step 2 - Dispatch

Spawn a general-purpose subagent. Give it, verbatim: the friction summary from
Step 1, and these instructions.

---

You are producing the end-of-phase status for {{PROJECT}}.

0. Resolve the interpreter FIRST and use it for every command below. If work
   happens in git worktrees, note that a virtualenv is usually gitignored and
   exists only in the main working tree, so a relative path will not resolve
   there. This finds it from either location, on any platform:

   ```sh
   MAIN="$(dirname "$(git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir)")"
   PY=""
   for c in "$MAIN/.venv/Scripts/python.exe" "$MAIN/.venv/bin/python" \
            "$MAIN/.venv/bin/python3"; do
       [ -x "$c" ] && PY="$c" && break
   done
   [ -n "$PY" ] || PY="$(command -v python3 || command -v python)"
   ```

   Substitute `$PY` wherever the commands below say `$PY`.

1. Run the collector:
   `$PY tools/extant_collect.py --collect --out status_bundle.json`

   **If the suite cannot run here, pass `--suite-json <path>`** with an
   already-captured result rather than repeating a long run. The collector stops
   with a RuntimeError naming that flag when it cannot find an interpreter for
   the configured suite command.

   The bundle records whether the suite figure was `measured` or `supplied`.
   Say which in the entry you draft - a reused count is not a fresh measurement.

   If `status_bundle.json` reports `nothing_to_hand_off` true, there are no
   commits since the last status: report that plainly and stop. Do not draft
   an entry, run `--archive`, or commit.

2. Read `status_bundle.json`. Prepend ONE new entry to `{{DOC}}`, above the
   existing entries and below the title. The entry's header must be EXACTLY of
   the form `{{ENTRY_PREFIX}}<n> - <title> (<status>, <date>)`. Any other header
   silently disables archiving and live-claim validation for that entry.
   Sections, in order:
   **Status**, **What Shipped**, **Known Issues**, **Next Tasks**, **Gotchas**.
   Fold the friction summary into Known Issues and Gotchas.

   You may only write claims the bundle supports. Do not estimate, infer a
   merge that the bundle does not show, or describe work you cannot see. If the
   suite is red, say so plainly in Status - a status that only describes green
   states lies exactly when the truth matters.

   If `plan.checkbox_tracking` is false, the plan's `remaining` list reflects
   an unmaintained file, not outstanding work - it MUST NOT be reported as
   such. Derive Next Tasks from the plan's prose and from `commits` instead.

3. Run the archiver, AFTER drafting: `$PY tools/extant_collect.py --archive`

   Order matters. Archiving before the new entry exists means the entry does
   not count toward the retention cap, so the document is left holding one more
   entry than the cap allows and the archive is permanently one cycle behind.
   Drafting first makes the new entry the newest, so the oldest is rotated out
   in the same run and the document holds exactly the retained count.

4. Validate:
   `$PY tools/extant_collect.py --validate {{DOC}}`
   Non-zero exit means fix the reported claims and re-run. **At most 2 attempts.**

   Fix claims by CORRECTING them, never by deleting them to pass. Report the
   findings from your FIRST validation run even if a later attempt cleared them.

5. If and only if validation exits 0, commit - and ONLY these paths:
   `{{DOC}}`, `{{ARCHIVE}}`, and any spec or plan doc you updated. Never source
   files. Never `--amend`. Never push.
   Message: `docs: status - <phase> complete at top of {{DOC}}`

   A RED SUITE DOES NOT BLOCK THIS COMMIT. Validation checks whether claims are
   true, not whether tests pass. A status that accurately records a failing
   suite is exactly what the next session needs; refusing to write one would
   withhold the truth at the moment it is most useful.

6. Report back: the commit SHA, retained/archived counts, suite result, and
   your first-run validation findings.

If validation still fails after 2 attempts, do NOT commit. Report the
outstanding findings and stop.

---

## Step 3 - Relay

Relay the subagent's report in 2-3 lines, including the first-run validation
findings even if they were later fixed.
